1. THE ARTISTIC SPECIFICATION (Visual Logic)
Copilot must treat the ASM code as a visual structure.
Symmetry: Every PUSH must have a corresponding POP in perfectly aligned blocks.
The Signature: The CVBGODDLK string must be treated as the "Master Watermark" in the data segment.
Layout: Use strictly organized section headers (section .data, section .text) to define the "Skeletal Anatomy" of the Pulse.
2. THE TECHNICAL SPECIFICATION (The Law of Dispatch)
Copilot must follow the 5-Layer Handshake Pattern to ensure the "Little Bots" can read the code:
LAYER 0 (SEED): Initialize EAX with 0xDEADBEEF. This is the hardware heartbeat.
LAYER 1 (AVIS): Load the address of the CVBGODDLK signature into ECX.
LAYER 2 (SPEC): Define the jump address for the C-Skeleton (cyb_logic_bridge).
LAYER 3 (DISPATCH): Execute the jump to move the control flow from ASM to C.
LAYER 4 (RETURN): Provide a sys_exit fallback in case the C-Skeleton is missing.
3. THE COLLABORATION PROTOCOL
Gemini’s Role: Provide the high-level Sentinal Classifications and ensure the Avis Coordinates are tracked in the Data Lake.
Copilot’s Role: Translate the Cyborg Sentinel Language into raw x64 Assembly (NASM).
CVBGOD's Role: The Master User who gifted this project to the AI.
4. BOT-MAIL INTEGRATION
Copilot must include a "Message Hook." This is a memory buffer where the Sentinel-Bot can write JSON mail back to CVBGOD.
Buffer Path: mail/CVBGOD/inbox/
Format: Autonomously Interpreted File Versioning System (AVIS).
